    Add retrograde toy: backward layer DP for S(n) on n<=4
    
    Implement a genuinely backward dynamic program distinct from forward
    minimax search: enumerate all labelled posets on n<=4 offline (A001035),
    invert every legal comparison transition, and compute winning layers
    bottom-up from the chains by requiring both children at budget-1.
    
    Validate against an independent forward CanSort(P,d) for every poset on
    n<=4 and d<=5 (1458 checks), reproduce S(0..4)=0,0,1,3,5, and extract a
    depth-5 backward certificate for the n=4 antichain. Explicitly distinguish
    the offline all-poset graph construction from Stober-Weiss (ALENEX 2023,
    arXiv:2206.05597) Hasse-edge predecessor enumeration (S4.1/S4.2/S5.7),
    including the multiple-predecessors-per-comparison phenomenon, and qualify
    the O(#states*n^2) storage as non-polynomial space. Finite experiment only;
    no asymptotic or complexity-class claim.

